  "explainer": "Net GEX estimates how many dollars of the underlying dealers would have to trade, under the sign assumption, for each 1% move. Compare it to how much normally trades: a few percent of daily volume is noticeable; a fraction of a percent is usually lost in normal flow. The size is a model estimate, not a measured flow.",
  "index_note": "Index products read larger than single stocks for four reasons: daily expiries keep a lot of short dated gamma open, index positioning is put heavy so less of it nets out, implied volatility is lower so each contract carries more gamma, and a 1% move is a large day for an index but a small one for a volatile stock. The per typical day view (1 ATR) puts them on a more equal footing."
